<</viewAble()/ModDate(D:20251218084921-08'00')/Subject(MPLS enables Enterprises and Service Providers to build and maintain networks that provide multiple services over a single infrastructure. You can integrate this economical solution over your existing infrastructure like IP, Ethernet, Frame Relay, and ATM. MPLS is independent of access technologies. So, you can aggregate subscribers with differing access links on an MPLS edge without changing your current environment.)/docType(TSD Products Configuration Guide Book)/Author(Unknown)/title(MPLS Configuration Guide for Cisco 8000 Series Routers, IOS XR Release 25.1.x, 25.2.x, 25.3.x, 25.4.x)/Campaigns()/alfrescoDocVersion()/date(2025-12-18T08:46:07.435-08:00)/concept(Cisco 8000 Series Routers)/Topics()/iaPath(cisco.com#Products#Cisco Products#Routers#Service Provider Core Routers#Cisco 8000 Series Routers)/Creator(DITA Open Toolkit)/Trapped/False/language(en)/CreationDate(D:20251218164526Z)/entitlementExpression(contains\( &quot;0,1,2,3,4,7&quot; , $profileField[3] \))/country(US)/secondaryConcept()/documentId(1743168146938790)/Title(MPLS Configuration Guide for Cisco 8000 Series Routers, IOS XR Release 25.1.x, 25.2.x, 25.3.x, 25.4.x)/contentType(cisco.com#US#postSales)/secondaryDoctype()/accessLevel(Customer,Guest,Partner)/Producer(XEP 4.30.961; modified using iText 2.1.7 by 1T3XT)/alfrescoTraceID()/fireWall()/downLoadable()/autoPlay()/description(MPLS Configuration Guide for Cisco 8000 Series Routers, IOS XR Release 25.1.x, 25.2.x, 25.3.x, 25.4.x)>>
